# Pin line endings: store LF in the repository and check LF out on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so without these attributes a
# windows-latest checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF. That is invisible on
# Linux/macOS (where the checkout stays LF) but breaks two Linux-first gates:
#
#   * `gofmt -l .` — gofmt emits LF, so a CRLF file is never "gofmt-clean" and
#     every .go file is reported as unformatted; and
#   * the knowledge base's strict YAML reader (kb/loader.go) — a bare `key:` line
#     arrives as `key:\r` and splitKey rejects it, so the whole KB fails to load.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect and leave binary files alone; `eol=lf` forces LF
# for everything it treats as text. Do not remove — see CONTRIBUTING.md.
* text=auto eol=lf
